SELECT 'bf-the-hyde-park-ckt-1', s.id, 'bf-the-hyde-park-survey', 'lighting', 'basement',
       55, 1600, 20, 24,
       'benchmark_confirmed', 'Basement',
       '2025-03-03'::date, '2025-03-23'::date,
       28.66, 64.47,
       jsonb_build_object('backfilled', true, 'source', 'signed agreement + post-installation savings report',
                          'note', 'Commissioned before this system existed — CON-16 eligibility was never assessed.',
                          'deviations', '["eligibility-never-assessed", "dates-inferred-from-readings", "benchmark-single-demo", "benchmark-adjusted-for-excluded-devices", "excluded-share-prorated-from-measured", "report-contradicts-its-own-table", "represented-count-mixes-fixture-types"]'::jsonb,
                          'basisNote', '63 tube lights on the circuit, of which 55 were replaced and 8 were not. THE EXCLUDED SHARE IS DEDUCTED PRO-RATA FROM THE MEASURED TOTAL, not by theoretical load: the report takes (28.66/63) x 8 = 3.64 kWh/day off, where Aditya Mega City and Arihant Arden both deduct count x wattage x hours. Different method, same intent. So the 55 lights'' figures are 25.02 before and 12.53 - 3.64 = 8.89 after, giving 16.13/25.02 = 64.4684% - the agreed 64.47%. baseline/after recorded here are the MEASURED whole-circuit totals 28.66 and 12.53, which ratio to 56.2805%, so the benchmark is an override. Same treatment as Aditya Mega City. Its post table''s own savings column (57.85, 57.54, 55.95, 56.91, 53.05) averages 56.26%, not the 64.47% printed in its Average cell - the column is against all 63 lights and the average is on the 55-light basis. Both tables reproduce their stated averages: 6 pre days 04-09 Mar 2025 average 28.6633 against 28.66, 5 post days 24-28 Mar average 12.5260 against 12.53. Neither date is stated: meter install taken as the day before the first pre-install reading (04 Mar 2025), replacement as the day before the post-install readings start (24 Mar).'),
       a.id, now()
FROM societies s, admin_users a WHERE s.name = 'The Hyde Park' AND a.id = 'sys-data-import' ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
